Hashmap - unsynchronized, not thread-safe, allows one null key and multiple null values. It is the most commonly used Map implementation.
Hashtable - synchronized, thread-safe, does not allow null keys or values. version of HashMap.
LinkedHashMap - maintains insertion order, allows one null key and multiple null values. It is a combination of HashMap and LinkedList.
TreeMap - sorted map, does not allow null keys, allows multiple null values. It is based on Red-Black Tree.


Map in general cannot contain duplicate keys,